Good morning,

There is currently drilling which is preventing me access and also welding
that produces a hazardous environment. Although the construction workers
are using gear and appear to be following healthy work and safety protocol
what about the effects on my health? The noise is above 120 dc and there
are toxic fumes being produced although the windows are opened a crack. How
can I do my laundry or use my storage unit when this is underway? Notice in
the video the inaccessibility.

The measurements of the storage unit are 90 cm x 60 cm x 60 cm. The door is
unlocked from 8:30 am until 4:30 pm each day of construction.

Please note that on form 8 the landlord has stated there will be no rent
reduction despite stating otherwise in emails to me. I assume you have
access to a copy.

Mr. Maclean, this landlord has engaged in deceptive practices and the
reasons are clear: Although the laundry and storage services have been
provided to me since my tenancy began in 2012, new tenants have not had the
services indicated in their lease agreements. The service of storage was
denied to new tenants without following proper protocol because the
landlord has had plans to do this two suite creation since 2018 upon
purchase of the property. Despite having the storage units available and
identified as correlated to individual suites (see photos in previous
emails) the landlord has left these services empty and were not provided to
tenants at no cost to themselves and with only the goal of making these
renovations as cheap as possible for themselves. Good business practices
would be to withdraw the services which are a *physical reality* by
following RTB protocol which was not done.  The tenants who have either
permitted or been deceived into permitting on suite renovations in which
their storage space was reduced further to make room for the laundry
services. The fact of the matter is that storage space in each of the
renovated units has been decreased and each of the tenants since 2018 have
been denied the storage unit services despite being available, accessible,
and clearly indicated as correlated to the tenant suites. Thorwin
Properties has engaged is deception and unethical treatment of their
tenants and all tenants affected should be reimbursed for these
self-serving practices. Let me be clear, there have been a reduction in
services provided to all tenants and yet rent increases have increased each
year which have deceptively not reflected the reduction in storage space in
each of the renovated tenants suites due to the laundry services being
installed and denial of storage unit services despite availability and
accessibility.

This company has exploited RTB protocol on technicality and this cannot be
allowed.

When you determine the amount of rent decrease that the withdrawal of
service of my unit will result in monthly I have an additional request:

Each of the tenants since 2018 have had access denied to services that have
been clearly identified on each of the now destructed storage units. I want
the RTB to recognize that service withdrawal protocol was not followed by
Thorwin, each of tenants should have had access to the associated storage
units as I have, and it would be prudent and just for the RTB to order
Thorwin Properties to retroactively payback the equivalent month by month
value of storage fees that are included in the rent amount paid by the
tenants from 2018 onwards.

I look forward to your response.

All the best,
Evan Rosner
